---
import { render } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { getArchive, formatDate, pathFor } from '../lib/archive';
const { anime, progress } = await getArchive();
const logs = await Promise.all(progress.map(async (entry) => ({ entry, ...await render(entry) })));
const stages = ['Source inspection', 'VapourSynth filtering', 'AV1 / HEVC encoding', 'Frame-by-frame QC', 'Audio & subtitle mux'];
---
<BaseLayout title="About Yuuki"><div class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Behind the archive</span><h1>A small archive.<br/>A careful process<span class="cyan">.</span></h1><p>[Yuuki] is a place to document the craft of encoding: what changed, why it changed, and what survived the encode.</p></div><div class="about-grid"><section class="philosophy panel"><Icon name="compare" size={22}/><h2>The frame comes first.</h2><div class="prose"><p>Lineart should stay clean. Gradients should stay quiet. Grain should retain its texture. A smaller file is useful only when it respects the source.</p><p>Each release keeps a source notebook, optional technical details, and room for comparisons. The guides make the workflow repeatable, and the benchmarks make its tradeoffs visible.</p><p>This v1 archive contains demonstration entries, local SVG illustrations, sample download links, and explicitly illustrative metric data. Replace them with your own measured work as the collection grows.</p></div></section><section class="pipeline panel"><span class="eyebrow">Reference workflow</span><h2>From source to release</h2><ol>{stages.map((stage, index) => <li><span class="mono">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>{stage}</li>)}</ol><p class="muted">Example bench: Windows or Linux, a modern multicore CPU, 32 GB+ RAM, and SSD scratch space. This describes a sample workflow, not a measured hardware configuration.</p></section></div><section class="progress-section" id="progress"><div class="section-heading"><h2><Icon name="activity"/> Activity log <span class="count">{logs.length}</span></h2><span class="mono subtle log-order">NEWEST FIRST</span></div><div class="timeline">{logs.map(({ entry, Content }) => { const related = anime.find((series) => series.id === entry.data.relatedAnime?.id); return <article class="log-entry"><time class="mono" datetime={entry.data.date.toISOString()}>{formatDate(entry.data.date)}</time><div class="log-content panel"><div class="pill-row"><span class="badge badge-violet">{entry.data.category}</span><span class:list={['badge', { 'badge-green': entry.data.stage === 'Completed' }]}>{entry.data.stage}</span>{related && <a href={pathFor('anime', related.id)} class="text-link">{related.data.title} ↗</a>}</div><h3>{entry.data.title}</h3><div class="prose"><Content/></div></div></article>; })}</div></section></BaseLayout>
<style>.about-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr; gap: 22px; } .philosophy, .pipeline { padding: 26px; } .philosophy > svg { color: var(--cyan); } h2 { margin-top: 16px; margin-bottom: 18px; } .pipeline h2 { margin-top: 12px; } .pipeline ol { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 20px 0; } .pipeline li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 11px 0; font-size: .85rem; } .pipeline li span { color: var(--cyan); font-size: .7rem; } .pipeline > p { font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.8; } .progress-section { margin-top: 34px; scroll-margin-top: 100px; } .section-heading h2 { margin: 0; } .log-order { font-size: .6rem; } .timeline { display: grid; gap: 18px; } .log-entry { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 115px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 20px; } .log-entry > time { color: var(--subtle); font-size: .7rem; padding-top: 18px; } .log-content { padding: 19px 22px; border-left: 2px solid var(--cyan); } .log-content h3 { margin: 13px 0 10px; } .log-content .prose { font-size: .85rem; } @media (max-width: 760px) { .about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .philosophy, .pipeline { padding: 20px; } .log-entry { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; } .log-entry > time { padding-top: 0; } }</style>
